  "narrative": {
    "top_frame": "Schlittler gave them a shutout. The bullpen finished the work. That's how you beat a division rival 2\u20130 with nine strikeouts and nothing to show for it offensively except two home runs.",
    "what_this_means": "Cam Schlittler was the story here. Six scoreless on one hit, eight strikeouts, complete command. Austin Wells and Ben Rice found fastballs they could handle and moved the game one swing at a time. Nothing elaborate, nothing desperate. The Yankees led from the first inning and never let it slip. This is what stabilizing looks like: one clear pitcher dominance, clean contact when it matters, and a bullpen that doesn't complicate things. Headrick, Blackburn, and Bednar covered the final three innings without argument. No drama needed. They won the game in the first and protected it for nine innings. That's a baseline the division doesn't usually wait around to beat twice.",
